hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15575","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Zufar al-Juhani narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Ashad al-Sulami narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I was seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he ordered us to gather for each man of us a dirham. So we bought a sacrifice for seven dirhams. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we made it expensive. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best sacrifices are the most expensive and the fattest. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and a man took a leg, and a man a leg, and a man a hand, and a man a hand, and a man a horn, and a man a horn, and the seventh slaughtered it, and we all made takbir over it."
